---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting started with kernic"
  description="Install kernic, generate your first design system, export tokens."
  active="start"
>
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p>
    kernic builds you a complete design system from the terminal: colors that work together,
    font pairings, text sizes, corner radii and gradients. You answer a few questions. It saves
    the result as plain JSON you own.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <p>Requires Node 20+.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="shell" code={`npm install -g kernic\n# or run instantly:\nnpx kernic`} />

  <h2>Generate a system</h2>
  <p>
    Running <span class="inline-kbd">kernic</span> opens Studio, the visual editor, in your
    browser. Prefer the terminal? <span class="inline-kbd">kernic wizard</span> walks you
    through the same thing: name, overall style ("vibe"), palette tuning with live color
    swatches, fonts, corner rounding and text sizes.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="shell" code={`kernic\n# or stay in the terminal:\nkernic wizard`} />
  <p>
    Systems are saved as plain JSON in <span class="inline-kbd">~/.config/kernic/systems/</span>.
    No account, no cloud. Just files.
  </p>

  <h3>Skip the wizard</h3>
  <CodeBlock lang="shell" code={`kernic create launch-page --vibe corporate --yes`} />

  <h2>Export tokens</h2>
  <p>Every format prints to stdout. Pipe it wherever it belongs:</p>
  <CodeBlock
    lang="shell"
    code={`# Tailwind v4 app.css\nkernic export midnight-neon -f tailwind > src/app.css\n\n# Plain CSS vars anywhere\nkernic export midnight-neon -f css >> styles/global.css\n\n# W3C design tokens for Terrazzo, Style Dictionary, Figma\nkernic export midnight-neon -f dtcg > design/tokens.json\n\n# DESIGN.md, tokens.json and shadcn.json for your agent and your app\nkernic context midnight-neon -o .\n\n# All of them at once\nkernic export midnight-neon -f all -o ./design-system`}
  />

  <h2>Tune it visually or by hand</h2>
  <p>
    Every export regenerates from the saved JSON. Tweak the file by hand, or open the
    local visual editor:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="shell" code={`kernic studio midnight-neon   # local web editor, 127.0.0.1 only`} />

  <div class="docs-callout">
    This very site is built that way: its <code>npm run build</code> runs
    <code>kernic export kernic-io -f css &gt; src/styles/tokens.css</code> before Astro compiles.
    No hand-written hex anywhere.
  </div>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/cli">Full CLI reference</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/tokens">What's inside the token files</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/agents">Point your AI coding agent at your system</a></li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
